<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Augustus Grant</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1827">1827</a>–<a href="/years/1892">1892</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Augustus Grant was a Scottish army officer and explorer who accompanied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-hanning-speke">John Hanning Speke</a> on the expedition of 1860–1863 to find the source of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>. In 1861 the pair stayed with King Rumanyika I of Karagwe, and their accounts made the kingdom known in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-augustus-grant.jpg" alt="James Augustus Grant" width="320" height="458" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ST-grant.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
